<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hong Kong</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hong Kong is a territory on the southern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. It was ceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-opium-war">First Opium War</a>, a symbol of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>'s humiliation by Western powers. It developed into a major British colonial port, and its handover to China in 1997 is often taken as the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hong-kong.jpg" alt="Hong Kong" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Designed by Tao Ho; SVG code of 24 November 2005 version copied from Open Clip Art; SVG code of 20 August 2011 version by Alkari … · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Hong_Kong.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
